1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,400
Cobi, a small AI core traveling through space,

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:06,600
is sent crashing to Earth by a sudden accident...

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:10,400
RoboLab is an MR laboratory where students restore a smart farm with Cobi
while learning robotics and coding.

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:14,900
Create an MR Robot Lab
Look at a desk or the floor. RoboLab detects a flat surface and creates your own robot lab.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:25,400
Explore Robot Components
Bring out each part from the control panel and learn what it does.

6
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:33,600
Assemble the Robot
Follow the example hologram to assemble the components and complete the robot.

7
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:41,900
Code on the Rule Board
Arrange rule blocks on the board to program the robot's behavior.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,900
Code on the Rule Board
Run the rule and check whether the robot behaves as intended.

9
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,900
Cobi, the AI Learning Partner
Instead of giving quick answers, Cobi asks questions that help students find their own solutions.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,400
Cobi, the AI Learning Partner
Students can speak through the hand-mounted microphone or tap a suggested question.

11
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:11,000
AI Inquiry Mode
After programming a robot, students can propose a new behavior and explore how to build it with Cobi.

12
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:22,900
MR Experiment Notes
Saved rules, experiment steps, and learning outcomes are recorded for later review.

13
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,100
Connected Web Experiment Notes
Notes saved in MR sync to the web for review on desktop or mobile.

14
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:42,100
Educator Dashboard
Educators can see student progress, difficult concepts, and how each rule evolved.

15
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:46,900
Physical Kit Integration
The web experiment notes connect to a physical robot kit made with 3D-printed parts.

16
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,800
Physical Kit Integration
Students can test how what they learned works on a real robot.
